{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/1798","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/1798/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/1798/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/1798/events","html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/1798","id":223998070,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMjM5OTgwNzA=","number":1798,"title":"Regression in client-side handling of error pages since v2.1.1","user":{"login":"gcpantazis","id":1161192,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjExOTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1161192?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcpantazis","html_url":"https://github.com/gcpantazis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcpantazis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcpantazis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcpantazis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcpantazis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcpantazis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcpantazis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcpantazis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcpantazis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcpantazis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2017-04-25T02:00:16Z","updated_at":"2018-05-11T18:05:27Z","closed_at":"2017-04-25T04:15:58Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":"resolved","sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"After upgrading to v2.2, I noticed that, on production builds, Next is rehydrating the routes for pages that errored during SSR. Steps to reproduce:\r\n\r\n1. Make a trivial page to trigger an error state:\r\n\r\n```\r\nimport React from 'react'\r\n\r\nexport default class NewTest extends React.Component {\r\n\r\n    static async getInitialProps({ res }) {\r\n        throw new Error('Test Error');\r\n\r\n        return {foo: 123};\r\n    };\r\n\r\n    render() {\r\n        return <div>\r\n            This page should always throw an error: {this.props.foo}\r\n        </div>\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n2. Navigate to this page via ` Link` on client-side. You should see the error page as anticipated.\r\n3. Refresh the page, allowing SSR to take over.\r\n\r\nObservations:\r\n* Error is displayed quickly, then is replaced by the output of `render()` in the view above.\r\n* `this.props.foo` is not filled, leading me to think `Next` is skipping `getInitialProps` for initial rehydration purposes, thus missing the error.\r\n* ...but, I wouldn't expect it to run this view at all if the server wasn't able to render it. I never want users to see a flash of content, and it makes tracking the issue more difficult.\r\n* Backing up to v2.1.1 fixes the issue, but I haven't isolated further than that.","closed_by":{"login":"arunoda","id":50838,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwODM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50838?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arunoda","html_url":"https://github.com/arunoda","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arunoda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arunoda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arunoda/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arunoda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arunoda/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arunoda/orgs","repos_url":